{"name":"Greywood","hex":"#9d9586","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"List of Reed College buildings","blocks":[{"text":"The Reed College campus includes academic buildings, dormitories and houses, administration and service buildings, student centers and other buildings. Academic buildings include the A. A. Knowlton Laboratory of Physics, Arthur F. Scott Laboratory of Chemistry (1992), Center for Advanced Computation, Educational Technology Center (2002), L.E. Griffin Memorial Biology Building, and Psychology Building. Buildings primarily used for the arts and performance include Kaul Auditorium, Studio Art Building, the Performing Arts Building, and Theatre Annex Building. The Annex features main stage and black box theaters with additional rooms for instruction and rehearsals, plus storage space sometimes called Reed Warehouse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Reed_College_Portland_OR_-_OpenStreetMap.png/330px-Reed_College_Portland_OR_-_OpenStreetMap.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Reed_College_buildings"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/AEDoyle-Master-Plan-1920.png/250px-AEDoyle-Master-Plan-1920.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/19/AEDoyle-Master-Plan-1920.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/AEDoyle-Master-Plan-1920.png/250px-AEDoyle-Master-Plan-1920.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A. E. Doyle's master plan (1920)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAEDoyle-Master-Plan-1920.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/28_West%2C_Reed_College.jpg/500px-28_West%2C_Reed_Co